Task README & Preview: MySQL RDS and EC2 Application Setup
Overview
This task successfully provisions a private MySQL RDS instance in AWS (us-east-1), configures network security groups for database access and web traffic, establishes passwordless SSH access to the xfusion-ec2 instance, and deploys a configured PHP connection script.

Architecture & Implementation Steps
1. Networking & Security Group Configuration
VPC Subnets: Discovered the default VPC (vpc-0f1d6a88ffd6ef17b) and generated an RDS DB subnet group (xfusion-rds-subnets) spanning all available subnets across the availability zones in us-east-1.

Security Groups:

EC2 Security Group (sg-0586eb60dff16a8dd): Configured ingress rules to open HTTP traffic on port 80 (0.0.0.0/0).

RDS Security Group (sg-0f71435f2e6024a50): Configured ingress rules to allow MySQL traffic on port 3306 originating exclusively from the EC2 security group.

2. RDS Instance Provisioning
Identifier: xfusion-rds

Engine & Version: MySQL 8.4.5

Instance Class: db.t3.micro

Storage: 5 GiB, gp2 storage type

Database Name: xfusion_db

Master User: xfusion_admin

Accessibility: Private (--no-publicly-accessible)

3. Passwordless SSH & File Deployment
Generated an RSA SSH key pair (/root/.ssh/id_rsa) on the aws-client host.

Pushed the public key using AWS EC2 Instance Connect and permanently appended it to /root/.ssh/authorized_keys on xfusion-ec2 (54.205.189.158).

Updated the template file /root/index.php using a Python automation snippet to inject the RDS endpoint, database name, username, and master password.

Securely copied the finalized index.php file to /var/www/html/index.php on the EC2 instance via SCP.

